        {
          "field_id": "database",
          "label": "Database",
          "control": "text"
        },
        {
          "field_id": "privilege",
          "label": "Privilege",
          "control": "text"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Hand-finished for the provider's native user and permission operations (/user, /user/changepermission, /user/changesqlprivileges): over the PostgreSQL wire GRANT and REVOKE are reported successes that do nothing (pkg/pgsql/server/stmts_handler.go:190). The record is the native /user/list entry with database_permissions and sql_privileges added by the provider. Round trip verified live on immudb 1.11.0 by tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_roundtrip_immudb.py (2026-10-31). Create a user, reopen its read-only state, change its password, grant and revoke a database permission and SQL privileges, deactivate and reactivate, drop (deactivates)."
}
